        "created_at": "2025-07-21T12:02:51.19164+00:00",
        "notes": "If you have 13000, pick Lumerico + 25 armor/shield. \n\nSo, [Speed Skates](item_521f3ef1-9acd-475e-8552-c6653c98cac9) is an experimental item, I only started picking it during my most recent games, but I've been surprised by how effective it was. What it does, is that after landing, you get 2 seconds during which as long as you stay on the ground, you're faster. It seems bad at first glance, but it has many great applications. It can A: help you get behind cover faster. Wall jumping is pretty bad at sharp turns. B: Help you fight someone who is in the open. If there are no walls around, you can't wall ride, and having 80% speed on the ground will make you very hard to hit. C: Avoid getting hit by a rocket or a sleep. It's pretty easy to predict where a Lucio who's jumping on you is going to end up. A Lucio who's slithering on the ground at 80% speed tho, much harder. D: Manoeuvre and fight enemies in tight spaces. No more hitting your head on some piece of geometry that steals all of your momentum.\n\nIf however you don't like the item, [#1 Single](item_5c5d5331-2966-440b-b989-aa92187eef97) or [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) are great picks in the same spot.\n\nYou may also be asking yourself: why so much health? Personally, the way that I think Lucio supports his team best, is by acting as kind of an off-tank where it's needed. You're not going to save people by healing them as Lucio, generally. You're going to save people by booping and bullying whoever is threatening them, and that requires being tanky. \n\nAlso, I'm not the most mindful player, I run into damage often, and if I died every time I made a mistake, I'd probably still be bronze (or whatever the equivalent is in this mode).",
