    {
        "id": "6521236d-0646-439a-8536-48a9c7289a5d",
        "build_id": "9c63021d-511a-4613-8321-25bfbb611082",
        "round_number": 6,
        "cash_earned": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-07-21T12:02:51.19164+00:00",
        "notes": "My rule for  [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) is that if you have had to use your beat often to prevent a team wipe, don't pick it, otherwise do pick it. So like, if their Genji has had a lot of value out of blade, or their Zarya with grav, you will want beat to stop them. \n\nOtherwise, Vanadium is too big of a boost to pass on. You don't need an ult if you are winning team fights on your own. And since it provides 50 shields, you don't need any other item to reach 100 combined armor/shield for Lumerico, which frees up some of your cash to get some weapon power.\n\nI put alternative epics that you can get instead if you don't like Vanadium.  [Sonic Recharger](item_c5e6a2c9-1bed-48fa-b539-01e76098a297) is a great health buff if you need it,  [Overdrive Core](item_a2a8dba1-5f2f-4da1-9445-b08f49162121) is a good item to pick if you really need to win a duel against let's say a mercy-pocketed soldier who is terrorizing your team, or if you're getting slept by Ana, and [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is just a great item overall.",
